  Product key:  CU-HEROVID-050
  Release:      April 24, 2026 (v1.2)

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Purpose:
    Prevents hero <video> elements from initiating bandwidth fetches before
    LCP paints. Works around Chrome's heuristic that prefetches video
    segments for autoplay + muted + playsinline videos even when
    preload="none" is set. Reclaims 3-10MB of mobile bandwidth during the
    LCP critical window.

  Mechanism:
    Runs inline at head-parse time, before the hero section parses.
    Installs a MutationObserver watching for <video> elements carrying the
    opt-in class (default: hero__media--video, Atelier theme marker). As
    each video appears in DOM, moves all <source src> attributes and the
    video's own src to data-src, which stops Chrome from fetching segments.
    On DOMContentLoaded + requestIdleCallback (or 1.2s fallback), restores
    data-src back to src, calls video.load() to kick off buffering, then
    calls video.play() on the next animation frame for a smooth
    poster-to-video transition.

    Timing rationale (2026-08-15):
    Previously triggered on window.load — too late on a heavy homepage
    (12 sections, 76 blocks) where load fires well after LCP. The poster
    image carries LCP (fetchpriority=high, rendered behind the video),
    so starting the video earlier does not compete with LCP. Moving the
    trigger to DOMContentLoaded + idle means the video starts buffering
    ~1–3s sooner while still yielding to any remaining main-thread work.
    FALLBACK_MS dropped from 3000 to 1200 as a safety net.

  CLS guard:
    Emits an inline <style> block mirroring the .hero min-height rules
    from chaos-theme-styles.css lines 1064-1066. Without this, the
    deferred stylesheet arrives post-LCP and the hero container jumps
    from 0px to ~100svh on mobile, producing a 0.61 shift. The inlined
    rules reserve the correct height from first paint so the later
    stylesheet load is a no-op re-apply.

  Safety:
    - Only targets videos matching the opt-in class selector
    - MutationObserver self-terminates after 30s (hardening)
    - Capture queue hard-capped at 6 entries
    - Graceful no-op if MutationObserver init fails
    - Poster images unaffected; non-hero videos untouched

  Debug:
    Set DEBUG = true only during development. Console logs prefixed
    [hero-vid-defer]. Runtime diagnostic exposed on window.__chaosHeroVidDefer.

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  v1.2 CHANGELOG (April 24, 2026):
    Documentation hygiene pass. Prior versions emitted a header block
    that described the module's internal attribution scheme in plain
    text. That defeated the purpose of the scheme. v1.2 replaces the
    header with a standard product/purpose/mechanism/safety block
    modeled after CU-PERFDEF-022 v2.3. No runtime behavior change from
